# Accessibility & Calm UX

## Accessibility
- Semantic HTML and correct heading hierarchy (one H1 per page).
- Keyboard navigation supported.
- Visible focus states (do not remove outlines without replacement).
- Icon-only buttons need aria-labels.
- Maintain readable contrast and font sizing.

## Calm UX
- Avoid intense animations, flashing, parallax.
- Prefer simple layouts and generous spacing.
- Mobile-first. Must work on low-end phones and poor connections.

## Language
- Architecture should allow Nepali and English content.
- Blog posts use `lang` in frontmatter; UI supports future language switch.